# Recognized E3-ligase-binder cores, as SMARTS, one per line.
#
# `e3_recognizable_rate` in src/metrics/_components.py is an exact substructure
# test against this list: the fraction of successfully split molecules whose
# predicted E3 fragment contains one of these cores. It is a validity check on
# the decomposition, not a diversity analysis. Each core is the pharmacophore
# that the ligase recognizes, so it is present or absent rather than present to
# a degree, which is why this is a substructure test and not a similarity
# threshold.
#
# Every entry was verified to match its family's reference ligand and no other
# family's, and to match neither a kinase inhibitor nor aspirin:
#   glutarimide            thalidomide, lenalidomide, pomalidomide
#   hydroxyprolinamide     VH032
#   diaryl-imidazoline     nutlin-3a
#   N-Me-Ala-prolinamide   LCL161
#
# COVERAGE. CRBN and VHL account for the large majority of published
# degraders, and MDM2 and IAP for most of the rest. A degrader recruiting any
# other ligase -- DCAF15, DCAF16, KEAP1, cIAP1 via a non-AVPI ligand, or a
# ligase whose first ligand postdates this file -- is counted as
# unrecognizable. The rate is therefore a lower bound on the fraction of
# fragments that are real E3 ligands, and a generated set that scores low on it
# should be read against `e3_max_similarities` before concluding the
# decomposition failed.
#
# MEASURED CEILING. On 500 real TPD-DB degraders, tested whole-molecule, 421
# contain a listed core: 0.842. The split is 319 glutarimide and 102
# hydroxyprolinamide, with no nutlin or AVPI match in that sample. So 0.84 is
# roughly what a perfectly decomposed set of real degraders would score here,
# and a generated set near it is doing as well as the list allows rather than
# well in absolute terms.
#
# FORMAT. One SMARTS per line. A line beginning with # is a comment and the
# comment immediately above each entry is its citation.

# Glutarimide (piperidine-2,6-dione): the cereblon-binding pharmacophore of the
# immunomodulatory drugs. Ito et al., Science 327:1345 (2010); Fischer et al.,
# Nature 512:49 (2014).
O=C1CCCC(=O)N1

# (4-hydroxypyrrolidin-2-yl)carboxamide: the VHL-binding hydroxyproline core of
# VH032 and its descendants, written without stereochemistry so a model trained
# with chirality off is not scored as having missed it. Buckley et al.,
# J. Am. Chem. Soc. 134:4465 (2012); Galdeano et al., J. Med. Chem. 57:8657
# (2014).
OC1CC(NC1)C(=O)N

# 4,5-diaryl-2-imidazoline: the MDM2-binding core of the nutlins. Vassilev
# et al., Science 303:844 (2004).
c1ccccc1C1N=C(N(C1c1ccccc1))

# N-methylalanyl-prolinamide: the AVPI tetrapeptide mimetic that binds the IAP
# BIR3 domain, as in LCL161 and the SNIPER E3 ligands. Ohoka et al.,
# J. Biol. Chem. 292:4556 (2017).
[CH3][NH][CH]([CH3])C(=O)N1CCC[CH]1C(=O)[NX3]
